        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computational Photography",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXPOSURE BRACKETING:\n    Capture N exposures (typically 3, 5, or 7) at different EVs\n    E.g., −2 EV, 0 EV, +2 EV (2-stop brackets)\n    Each exposure optimal for different tonal range:\n      −2 EV → highlights (sky, sun) properly exposed\n       0 EV → midtones\n      +2 EV → shadows (dark interior) properly exposed\n    Merge: select best-exposed values per pixel → linear HDR image"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:photography:08-computational-photography, git-history:photography:08-computational-photography]",
        "canonical_path": "photography/08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md",
        "concepts": "[computational, photography]",
        "current_path": "photography/08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md",
        "id": "maxim:photography:computational-photography",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "photography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[computational, photography]",
        "section": "photography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computational Photography",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GHOSTING:\n    Moving objects (clouds, water, people) appear in different positions across brackets\n    → Appear as transparent ghost when images merged\n    Deghosting: for each pixel, detect if the value is inconsistent with reference frame\n      → Reject outlier values; use reference frame instead\n    Modern deghosting (Lightroom, PTGui): motion detection per region → smart selection\n    Limitation: fast motion + large brackets → deghosting artifacts"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md#014",
      "path": [
        "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:photography:08-computational-photography, git-history:photography:08-computational-photography]",
