        "section": "photography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computational Photography",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SINGLE-FRAME HDR (modern sensors):\n    Dual gain readout: each pixel read at two amplification levels simultaneously\n    Or: dual exposure (interleaved rows/frames at 2 different ISOs)\n    → No ghosting (single moment capture)\n    → Less total DR than bracketed but avoids motion issues"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md"
      ],
