      },
      "text": "Reinhard (2002) — most influential:\n    Luminance mapping: L_d = L_w / (1 + L_w)\n    Automatic: 0 → 0; large L_w → 1.0 (asymptote)\n    Extended Reinhard: adds \"white point\" parameter Lwhite\n      L_d = L_w × (1 + L_w / Lwhite²) / (1 + L_w)\n    Property: very bright highlights → compressed; midtones → preserved\n    Visual: natural; loses some \"pop\"; popular for real-world photography"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md#020",
      "path": [
        "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md"
      ],
