      },
      "text": "BILATERAL TONE MAPPING (Durand 2002):\n    Decompose image into base layer (large-scale luminance) + detail layer\n    Compress only the base layer (reduces large dynamic range)\n    Preserve + add back detail layer (maintains local contrast)\n    → Result: feels more \"real\"; local contrast preserved; no halos if done well\n    Halo artifact: if base/detail decomposition is imperfect → dark ring around bright areas"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COMPUTATIONAL-PHOTOGRAPHY.md#024",
      "path": [
