        "root_concepts": "[computational, photography]",
        "section": "photography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computational Photography",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FOCUS STACK WORKFLOW:\n  1. Capture N frames (same position; change focus by known step)\n     Step size: depends on DoF at each magnification/aperture; usually automated\n  2. Align frames: even on tripod, small vibrations cause pixel-level shifts\n     ECC alignment (enhanced correlation coefficient) or feature-based\n  3. Depth map estimation: assign depth to each pixel based on focus stack\n  4. Fusion: blend pixels from appropriate depth frames"
    },
    {
